n><img alt=\"Drowning Icon Big\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Drowning_Icon_Big_f65e47.gif\" width=\"16\"/></span></span></div><div class=\"creature-resistance-bar1\"><div class=\"creature-resistance-bar2\" style=\"border-width:1px 0 1px 1px; width:0.0000%; background-color:#ff3333; left:0.0000%;\"></div><div class=\"creature-resistance-pct\" style=\"position:absolute; left:calc(5px + 100% * 0.0000); display:inline-block;\">0%</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"creature-resistance-el\" data-value=\"1.0000\" title=\"Healing\"><div class=\"creature-resistance-label\">Healing <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Healing Icon\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Healing_Icon_be4df6.gif\" width=\"16\"/></span></span></div><div class=\"creature-resistance-bar1\"><div class=\"creature-resistance-bar2\" style=\"border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; width:90.9091%; background-color:#ffffff; left:0.0000%;\"></div><div class=\"creature-resistance-pct\" style=\"position:absolute; right:calc(5px + 9.0909%); display:inline-block;\">100%?</div></div></div>\n</div><div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-location\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Location\">Location</span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"#/wiki/Pits%20of%20Inferno\">Pits of Inferno</a> - <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Ruthless%20Seven\">Ashfalor</a>'s Throneroom.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-behaviour\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Behaviour\">Behaviour</span></h3>\n<p>\tBehaves just like a regular <a href=\"#/wiki/Undead%20Dragon\">Undead Dragon</a>, except that it is much stronger. It also runs in low health.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-strategy\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Strategy\">Strategy</span></h3>\n<p>\tTreat it like a regular <a href=\"#/wiki/Undead%20Dragon\">Undead Dragon</a>, just keep in mind it can do very high comboes. Have a <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knight</a> stand diagonal, a <a href=\"#/wiki/Druid\">Druid</a> to heal the <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knight</a> and as many Mages and <a href=\"#/wiki/Paladin\">Paladins</a> shoot at <b>Dracola</b>.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div class=\"history-section\" id=\"w-creature-history\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-History\">History</span></h3>\n<p>This dragon was first introduced in the game 1997 when a map hacker added this creature in to the map in a hidden pick spot in the <a href=\"#/wiki/Plains%20of%20Havoc\">Plains of Havoc</a> Dragon Lair, Guido later discovered the dragon and removed it admittedly.\n</p><p>This creature re-appeared in the 7.9 Update, and can be found as a rare spawn in the <a href=\"#/wiki/Pits%20of%20Inferno\">Pits of Inferno</a>.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Loot\">Loot</span></h3>\n<p><small><i>Drop rates are estimated based on 23 samples <span class=\"loot-stats-link\">(Loot Statistics)</span>.</i></small> <small><i>Colour-coding is applied after 50 samples — current sample size is below this threshold.</i></small><br/><small><i>Task column indicates items used in delivery tasks.</i></small>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align:center; width:auto;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Task</th>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Avg</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">%\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"loot-table-icon\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Dracola's Eye\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Dracola_s_Eye_6dd289.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span></span></td>\n<td>Dracola's Eye</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1.0</td>\n<td class=\"\" data-sort-value=\"100.000000\" style=\"text-align:center;\">100%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"loot-table-icon\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"